0 s"Subgen. Echinoramaria" Spores echinulate; saprobes growing on conifer needles or leaves, rarely on thin branches (fruitbodies often rather tough and thin-fleshed with ±brownish or greenish colours). 011260 Subgen. Echinoramaria, page 10 37
0 Spores smooth, striate or verrucose; saprobes or mycorrhizal0113702
0s" Subgen. Lentoramaria" Rhizomorphs dimitic or fruitbodies growing on wood; saprobes; fruitbodies often rather tough and thin-fleshed. 023480 Subgen. Lentoramaria, page 8 30
0s" Subgen. Ramaria" Rhizomorphs, if present, monomitic; mycorrhizal or rarely saprobes, growing on needles or leaves; fruitbodies often soft and ±fleshy. 023590 Subgen. Ramaria, page 23
